cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "cardid: Entity Resolution for Sports Trading Card Listings"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ioannis Filippos"
    family-names: "Kanellopoulos"
    email: "i.f.kanellopoulos@tilburguniversity.edu"
    affiliation: "Tilburg University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0062-0889"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jk2049/cardid"
abstract: >-
  An R package for resolving unstructured sports trading card listings into
  structured identifiers. Given the free-text title and product information of a
  basketball or baseball trading card, cardid identifies the player and the year
  the card refers to and constructs a standardised card identifier, enabling
  listings to be matched across marketplaces and over time. The package was
  developed to build the analysis panel for research on the effect of
  non-fungible tokens on physical collectibles markets, and is reusable for any
  setting requiring entity resolution of marketplace listing text.
keywords:
  - entity resolution
  - record linkage
  - trading cards
  - collectibles
  - digital markets
  - non-fungible tokens
  - R
